WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:09.210
Caroline Aghajanian: On this
episode of "Travel Dares,"

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:10.920
Aj Caldwell: I'm taking
Caroline to Zip World

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:13.500
to try the world's fastest zip line.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.930
Caroline: And I'm here at
the Pontcysyllte Aqueduct,

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:19.330
where we're gonna canoe
126 feet in the air.

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:20.990
Come join us on our adventures

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:23.383
on this episode of "Travel Dares!"

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:28.420
Welcome to "Travel Dares!"

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.160
I'm Caroline, and in this episode,

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:32.400
we're in Wales with my friend Aj.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.546
Aj: Wales is known for
its rolling countryside

00:00:34.546 --> 00:00:36.480
and rich history, with some of the most

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:38.710
picturesque landscapes you'll ever see.

00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:40.540
Caroline: I use my Marriott
Bonvoy Boundless card

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.450
on all of my trips so that I can earn

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:44.949
two times the points on
my everyday purchases.

00:00:44.949 --> 00:00:46.640
Aj, how excited are you?

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:48.030
Aj: I am so excited!

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:49.420
Are you ready for your first clue?

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:51.003
Caroline: So ready.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:55.569
OK, very clever.

00:00:55.569 --> 00:00:58.154
Oh, I hope I have a helmet for this, Aj,

00:00:58.154 --> 00:00:59.487
if it's head-first.

00:00:59.487 --> 00:01:01.630
Aj: You'll be OK.

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:03.070
Caroline: I don't know, "head first"?

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:06.418
I don't know, I feel like
you are very adventurous,

00:01:06.418 --> 00:01:09.262
so I feel like we might be bungee jumping.

00:01:09.262 --> 00:01:11.917
Aj: Caroline's never done
anything like this before,

00:01:11.917 --> 00:01:14.483
and even though it'll be
a little intimidating,

00:01:14.483 --> 00:01:16.220
it's the perfect way to push her

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:17.420
out of her comfort zone.

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:20.090
I'm gonna set you right there.

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:21.320
You stay there.
Caroline: Oh, my gosh.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:22.550
I feel like we're really high up.

00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:23.560
There's a railing.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:25.560
Aj: Uh, you know.
(zips zipper)

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:26.690
Caroline: You're wearing
something, you're definitely

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:28.571
wearing something. That
was a zipper. Oh, my gosh.

00:01:28.571 --> 00:01:29.540
Aj: You can take your blindfold off.

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:30.662
Caroline: OK, OK.

00:01:30.662 --> 00:01:32.862
Aj: Because we're going down
the world's fastest zip line.

00:01:32.862 --> 00:01:34.397
Caroline: Oh, my gosh!

00:01:34.397 --> 00:01:36.897
Oh, my gosh!

00:01:36.897 --> 00:01:37.730
What?

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:40.560
I'm so, this is so high up.

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:49.602
Tim Pennington: Zip World's Velocity 2

00:01:49.602 --> 00:01:50.570
is the most unique ride.

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:52.960
It's the longest ride in
the Northern Hemisphere.

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:54.057
We have got the world record

00:01:54.057 --> 00:01:55.610
for the fastest zip line in the world.

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:57.952
We've broken that record twice, now.

00:01:57.952 --> 00:02:00.480
The zip line takes
approximately 56 seconds

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:03.403
to do one mile and drop over 1,200 feet.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.070
Aj: All right. How do I look?

00:02:07.070 --> 00:02:07.903
Caroline: You look great! How do I look?

00:02:07.903 --> 00:02:09.130
Aj: You look good, too.

00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:09.963
Caroline: Woo!

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:14.551
We are on our way to the big boy.

00:02:14.551 --> 00:02:15.643
Aj: The big one!

00:02:15.643 --> 00:02:19.122
Caroline: It is, uh. Yeah,
we're just a tad bit nervous.

00:02:19.122 --> 00:02:21.563
Aj: Eh, just a little bit.

00:02:21.563 --> 00:02:23.460
But you know what? No turning back now.

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:24.802
We have to do it.

00:02:24.802 --> 00:02:27.360
It literally feels like
we're on top of the world.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:29.782
This is so breathtaking.

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:32.076
Oh, my gosh!
Aj: Look at them!

00:02:32.076 --> 00:02:34.780
Caroline: They're going so fast!

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:36.050
You know what, I just
can't think about it.

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:36.960
I just have to go.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:38.091
Let's just go.
Aj: Let's do it.

00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:38.924
Caroline: Let's do it, let's do it!

00:02:38.924 --> 00:02:40.150
Aj: Let's do it!

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:41.470
Caroline: OK.

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:43.640
Here I go. OK.

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:44.727
Oh, my gosh, OK.

00:02:44.727 --> 00:02:48.350
I think I'm just getting strapped in now.

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:49.650
Aj, where are you?

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:50.833
Aj: I'm over here.

00:02:50.833 --> 00:02:52.430
Caroline: Getting strapped in.

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:53.263
Uh-oh.

00:02:53.263 --> 00:02:56.370
It's a lot higher from this angle.

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:57.378
Aj: Here we go.

00:02:57.378 --> 00:02:58.211
(laughing)

00:02:58.211 --> 00:02:59.280
Here we go.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:01.046
Caroline: It's like we're levitating!

00:03:01.046 --> 00:03:02.219
Aj: I know!

00:03:02.219 --> 00:03:03.202
Instructor: Safeties on.

00:03:03.202 --> 00:03:04.035
Caroline: Uh-oh.

00:03:04.035 --> 00:03:06.096
Instructor: All right, let's go, guys.

00:03:06.096 --> 00:03:09.422
OK, three, two, one.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:11.755
(screaming)

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:34.639
Aj: Yeah!

00:03:34.639 --> 00:03:35.793
Caroline: That was so much fun!

00:03:35.793 --> 00:03:36.903
The view!

00:03:36.903 --> 00:03:38.850
When you first, like,
step off the platform,

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:41.120
it feels like this is the end.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.760
It's the last thing you're gonna see.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:44.871
And then you start picking up speed,

00:03:44.871 --> 00:03:46.680
and it just gets so much better.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:50.062
It just gets, like, so relaxing
and you just get to sit

00:03:50.062 --> 00:03:52.763
and just stare at the view around you.

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:56.673
Aj, that was so much fun!

00:03:56.673 --> 00:03:58.307
Thank you so much for bringing me here.

00:03:58.307 --> 00:04:00.033
Aj: Caroline, you were so brave today,

00:04:00.033 --> 00:04:01.160
I'm so impressed.

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:04.020
Caroline: Everyone talks about
how Wales is so beautiful,

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:07.247
and, honestly, I think this
is the best way to see it.

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:08.610
Aj, your clue.

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:10.235
Aj: All right, here we go.

00:04:13.090 --> 00:04:14.833
So we're going up high, it's heights.

00:04:14.833 --> 00:04:17.370
Caroline: Uh, you just
have to wait and see

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:18.944
until we get there.
Aj: OK, so it's gonna be,

00:04:18.944 --> 00:04:21.213
like, skydiving?

00:04:23.690 --> 00:04:25.040
Don't look down?

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:27.460
I think we're gonna like,
dangle off something

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:28.935
or be pushed off something

00:04:28.935 --> 00:04:30.740
or jump off something really high?

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:33.020
Caroline: Aj loves thrill
rides, and the combination

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:35.280
of the intense height
with the zen activity

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:37.410
is something he's never done before.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:39.590
This adventure is gonna be the perfect way

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:42.063
for Aj to see the Welsh countryside.

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:46.900
Aj: All right.
Caroline: All right.

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:49.030
OK, you stand here.

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:50.980
Take off your blindfold,

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:52.440
'cause we are going canoeing

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:54.650
over 120 feet in the air!

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:55.785
Aj: Are you kidding?

00:04:55.785 --> 00:04:56.793
This is so cool!

00:04:56.793 --> 00:04:59.023
Caroline: And we're
headed in that direction.

00:05:06.103 --> 00:05:07.395
Andy Turton: All right then, welcome

00:05:07.395 --> 00:05:08.994
to the Pontcysyllte Aqueduct.

00:05:08.994 --> 00:05:10.681
So, are you guys ready to go?

00:05:10.681 --> 00:05:11.664
Aj: Yeah, I'm ready!
Caroline: Yeah,

00:05:11.664 --> 00:05:13.320
I'm totally ready. Let's do it!

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:15.787
Andy: Brilliant. This is an amazing way

00:05:15.787 --> 00:05:18.053
to get quite a thrill-seek,

00:05:18.053 --> 00:05:20.563
from going canoeing on a canal

00:05:20.563 --> 00:05:23.930
to then paddle 126 foot above the river,

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:27.557
with the sheer sideage,
to look over is quite,

00:05:27.557 --> 00:05:29.800
quite impressive to be able to do.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:31.900
It's great that we've got
it to be able to do it here.

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:33.739
Caroline: Pro tip: Don't fall, yeah.

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:36.131
Aj: All right.

00:05:36.131 --> 00:05:38.083
Caroline: OK, we just
can't shake the boat, Aj.

00:05:38.083 --> 00:05:39.964
Aj: Yeah, don't rock the boat.

00:05:39.964 --> 00:05:41.450
Caroline: Lean!

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:44.045
Aj: I'm very excited,
I'm a little nervous,

00:05:44.045 --> 00:05:45.787
but I'm really excited to see this view.

00:05:46.747 --> 00:05:48.780
Caroline: All right, and we're...

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:53.030
Aj: I think I hear, like, a stream?

00:05:53.030 --> 00:05:54.650
Caroline: Yeah, same.

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:56.360
Oh, it's a river!

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:57.785
Aj: It's a river below us!

00:05:57.785 --> 00:05:59.020
Caroline: We're paddling.

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:00.700
Aj: We're paddling over a river.

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:01.533
Caroline: Over a river.

00:06:01.533 --> 00:06:03.222
We're on a river, on a river.

00:06:03.222 --> 00:06:04.430
Aj: I wanna, you wanna look over?

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:05.890
Caroline: We're on the
big boy bridge. Yeah.

00:06:05.890 --> 00:06:07.425
Aj: I wanna look over here.

00:06:07.425 --> 00:06:09.170
Caroline: Uh-oh, we're getting risky!

00:06:09.170 --> 00:06:11.323
We're getting risky here, Aj!

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:16.670
Aj: Oh, my gosh.

00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:17.503
Look at this.

00:06:17.503 --> 00:06:18.610
Caroline: Wow.

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:20.630
We are higher than the birds right now.

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:22.040
Aj: We are literally
higher than the birds.

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:23.330
There's birds flying below us.

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:24.230
Caroline: This is beautiful.

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:25.970
Lynda Slater: It's the
highest and the longest

00:06:25.970 --> 00:06:28.060
in Great Britain, of the aqueducts.

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:30.750
It's obviously been
standing for over 200 years.

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:33.040
It's a significant feat of engineering.

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:35.980
It's why it's been, dominated
all the World Heritage Sites.

00:06:35.980 --> 00:06:37.617
In fact, we're celebrating
10 years of having

00:06:37.617 --> 00:06:40.020
World Heritage Site
subscription this year.

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:43.272
Aj: You know, I think the
views here and at Zip World

00:06:43.272 --> 00:06:46.355
are two of the most beautiful
views you can see in Wales.

00:06:46.355 --> 00:06:47.800
Caroline: Honestly, I think this is one of

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:50.045
the most serene views I've ever seen.

00:06:50.045 --> 00:06:51.945
Aj, did you have a good time?

00:06:51.945 --> 00:06:52.953
Aj: Oh, it was dope!

00:06:52.953 --> 00:06:54.120
I loved it so much.

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:55.486
Caroline: I'm so glad.

00:06:58.070 --> 00:07:00.260
I had such an amazing time in Wales.

00:07:00.260 --> 00:07:01.740
It was both of our first time here,

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:04.570
and it was way more beautiful
than I thought it would be.

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:07.120
Aj: There is no better way
to end our UK experience

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:08.675
than with a nice cup of tea

00:07:08.675 --> 00:07:09.850
back at the hotel.

00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:12.660
Caroline: This is actually
the oldest hotel in Bristol.

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:14.760
It's, like, 150 years old.

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:16.560
Aj: Really? That's very classy.

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:18.830
Caroline: Aj, how do you
think I did on my dare?

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:20.242
Aj: Well, when I revealed
that we were going

00:07:20.242 --> 00:07:21.805
down the world's fastest zip line,

00:07:21.805 --> 00:07:23.432
I really thought you were gonna be scared,

00:07:23.432 --> 00:07:25.343
but you were actually really excited,

00:07:25.343 --> 00:07:26.990
even when we got to the
top of the mountain,

00:07:26.990 --> 00:07:30.470
staring down 1,500
meters of zip-line cable.

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:32.500
You were excited and ready to go.

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:33.742
So, for that,

00:07:33.742 --> 00:07:36.051
I'm giving you five out of five stars.

00:07:36.051 --> 00:07:37.420
Caroline: Yes!

00:07:37.420 --> 00:07:40.515
I love a good five out of five stars.

00:07:40.515 --> 00:07:41.920
Thank you, no, it was really fun.

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:44.350
It was such an exhilarating feeling

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:45.580
and the views were beautiful,

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:47.870
so I really, really did enjoy it.

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:49.690
Aj: Caroline, I had a great time,

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:51.800
but I have to know, what is my rating?

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:54.600
Caroline: OK, so, honestly,
Aj, I was really impressed

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:56.870
with how well you handled this dare.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:58.761
You went straight to the front of the boat

00:07:58.761 --> 00:08:00.430
and you canoed really well,

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:02.220
and you even looked over the bridge

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:03.890
and you weren't even scared.

00:08:03.890 --> 00:08:06.160
So, for those reasons, Aj, you're getting

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:07.720
a five out five stars!

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:09.512
Aj: Yes, that's what I wanted!

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:13.580
Caroline: Aj, finish your tea

00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:15.620
because we have a flight to catch.

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:17.620
Aj: I am so ready for this next dare.

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:18.992
Caroline: Pinkies up.

00:08:18.992 --> 00:08:19.909
(clink)

